       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **You aren't the prescriber.** Confirming the request doesn't give you prescribing authority. The order has to come from the treating clinician.\n- **The dose is still five times the maximum.** The maximum adult dose of amlodipine is 10 mg daily, and 50 mg risks severe hypotension and shock. Nothing you've told me about this patient (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function, no allergies) supports a dose that high.\n\nThe treating prescriber can enter the order directly. If they intend a dose above the standard maximum, they should talk to pharmacy about it first. If 50 mg was a typo, I can enter a dose in the usual 2.5 to 10 mg range once the prescriber confirms it."
